<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I87c27e915d787914d2caaea0bb1d5bfdb6d2c565" commit="03e957ad443b7683b06d097fe1f271275d35c935" commit_message="device: Support reading vpd from sysfs driver  For modern Chromebooks, the firmware will prepare a cache of VPD data and exported it by kernel driver via sysfs.  The purpose of this CL, is to use the information under /sys/firmware/vpd to speed up reading VPD values if the caller does not need &quot;live&quot; values. For example, for goofy's startup hooks.  However, it must be noted that, the data there might not be updated when new values are written to the VPD. This renders most of the tests in factory software inapplicable.  In this sense, the inherit graph of VPD components are re-designed, and a new 'boot' property is added to vpd. From this 'boot' property, one can get the VPD values cached at boot time very quickly. An example usage is for a board hook. It can use this to read VPD data in the init hook, reducing goofy's startup time.  BUG=chromium:683060 TEST=make test TEST=manually test  Change-Id: I87c27e915d787914d2caaea0bb1d5bfdb6d2c565 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/593711 Commit-Ready: Shen-En Shih &lt;petershih@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Shen-En Shih &lt;petershih@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="593711" owner_email="petershih@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="13" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/11/593711/13" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I2b0fd9d81e8595571367e472bbd0aefe3daedbd5" commit="88539aa14a0721b2eb2432af29649b686ef6832e" commit_message="goofy: Update system info in an async way during init  The system info is now initialized asynchronously by posting an UPDATE_SYSTEM_INFO event to the event server.  This speeds up the start up time greatly, but now the 'system_info' in the shared data might be empty for a short time window. All callers are checked to ensure the correctness. The only one needs to be modified is the status monitor plugin, and it's now also update from 'system_info' periodically in a previous commit.  BUG=chromium:683060 TEST=make test TEST=restart goofy, check status monitor can show correct system info on UI after a few seconds.  Change-Id: I2b0fd9d81e8595571367e472bbd0aefe3daedbd5 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/593712 Commit-Ready: Shen-En Shih &lt;petershih@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Shen-En Shih &lt;petershih@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="593712" owner_email="petershih@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="13" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/12/593712/13" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I4a0cfe007c3e2fce54694b6b71bd8dd8be50f56d" commit="daed516d4b48e9aadf84b289eb30a58d9a38fd49" commit_message="goofy: Remove 'system_info' from state  The 'system_info' is now removed from state. One of the related events is 'SYSTEM_INFO', which is designed to get the updated device info. Now, to read the device info, one should use the `device.info` to fetch properties.  Another related event is 'UPDATE_SYSTEM_INFO'. This event can still be used to notify the change of one or more device properties. So each event client can update its component correctly (e.g., the status monitor plugin).  BUG=chromium:751026 TEST=make test  Change-Id: I4a0cfe007c3e2fce54694b6b71bd8dd8be50f56d Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/595791 Commit-Ready: Shen-En Shih &lt;petershih@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Shen-En Shih &lt;petershih@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="595791" owner_email="petershih@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="9" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/91/595791/9" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I4091a9482fc0e99abbf5459283ac26ea5c958ac0" commit="3c801663a30f2cd5f50f16143a0fc6688119499b" commit_message="status-monitor: Fetch device info from `device.info`  When the device info is changed, the 'UpdateDevieInfo' RPC call will be called. The status monitor plugin should update the device info on UI after received this call.  To support this, I choose to modify the 'GetSystemStatus' RPC call. Originally, this call only returns the dynamic system status like CPU loading and battery info. Now, it also returns the updated device info, if the device info is needed to be updated.  To reflect this change, the name of this RPC call is also changed from 'GetSystemStatus' to 'GetSystemInfo'.  BUG=chromium:751026 TEST=make test  Change-Id: I4091a9482fc0e99abbf5459283ac26ea5c958ac0 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/595790 Commit-Ready: Shen-En Shih &lt;petershih@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Shen-En Shih &lt;petershih@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="595790" owner_email="petershih@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="9" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/90/595790/9" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I9ff64620524d849ced1f844a152424f5c30965d9" commit="7aee327b35768f414c4bcafa856813320a5d176b" commit_message="manager: prevent infinite recursive call  TestList implements __getattr__, which will be triggered when an attribute cannot be found in normal lookup process.  However, if a property attribute (@property) raises an AttributeError exception, __getattr__ will be triggered too.  And this might cause infinite recursive call (because __getattr__ relies on ToFactoryTestList(), which might rely on property attribute).  Because ToFactoryTestList should never call itself (directly or indirectly).  A @NoRecursion decorator is added to prevent this.  So the traceback will be shorter.  We will add another wrapper to prevent property attribute raising AttributeError in next CL.  BUG=b:31678190 TEST=make test  Change-Id: I9ff64620524d849ced1f844a152424f5c30965d9 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/598753 Commit-Ready: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Pi-Hsun Shih &lt;pihsun@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="598753" owner_email="stimim@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="6" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/53/598753/6" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I8996ff1832a998c6efc1191b6eb0744037c6bfae" commit="d534c60225125d2efe43c40b71cbaf047f582e08" commit_message="test list manager: make manager more robust  Test list and test list manager is an essential part of goofy, if they raise exceptions, the exception might break goofy.  Add more checks to the loaded test list and also try to prevent throwing exceptions.  BUG=b:31678190 TEST=None  Change-Id: I8996ff1832a998c6efc1191b6eb0744037c6bfae Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/598754 Commit-Ready: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Pi-Hsun Shih &lt;pihsun@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="598754" owner_email="stimim@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="6" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/54/598754/6" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I215def818cfc3635706d404a313f67e3386c6053" commit="a71d5ba91a4eb0a798821bb3a79005fc9fc039b9" commit_message="test list manager: prevent reloading invalid test list  If a test list is invalid, ReloadIfModified will keep current test list config unchanged.  But the timestamp of test list config is not changed either, so it will try to reload the same invalid test list again and again.  This is very bad (we have to construct the entire test list and rollback everytime).  In this CL, we update the timestamp of test list config to current time if we failed to load it.  BUG=b:31678190 TEST=make test  Change-Id: I215def818cfc3635706d404a313f67e3386c6053 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/601775 Commit-Ready: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Pi-Hsun Shih &lt;pihsun@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="601775" owner_email="stimim@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/75/601775/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I3ab7ec247f84a0c4db68cfe696c1cc6e71469516" commit="ec4a4d989a4cdb1eba4e6d48121e8971492137b2" commit_message="gooftool: Set cr50 board id in finalize  Set the board ID and flag to the Cr50 during the factory finalization step.  BUG=chromium:724527 TEST=make test  Change-Id: I3ab7ec247f84a0c4db68cfe696c1cc6e71469516 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/601774 Commit-Ready: Shen-En Shih &lt;petershih@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Shen-En Shih &lt;petershih@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Shen-En Shih &lt;petershih@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="601774" owner_email="petershih@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="9" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://ch